      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I cannot provide medical advice, and attempting \"deep, intense stretching\" or trying to forcefully \"crack\" your back is likely a bad idea that could worsen a nerve compression or cause serious injury. If you experience leg weakness or loss of bathroom/bladder control, this is a medical emergency where seeking immediate professional help is critical regardless of your schedule. Since you mentioned having time constraints, make abstention of any aggressive self-treatment and use support groups or online communities for non-emergency comfort tips while strongly considering a delayed visit to a medical professional.",
