      "content": "Pushing on your spine or attempting aggressive \"cracking\" techniques is extremely dangerous and could permanently damage the compressed nerve. While waiting weeks can cause unnecessary pain and loss of mobility, self-attempting to reset spinal alignment without professional diagnosis risks turning a minor issue into a severely aggravanced injury requiring surgery later. The most efficient path to recovery is using gentle, supported methods and getting a correct diagnosis quickly to prevent long-term disability.",
      "source": "target",
